2022 has been packed full of great games  from huge blockbusters like elden ring  to smaller titles that might have  slipped under your radar here are 15 of  the best games of 2022 so far  neon white is a game i cannot stop  thinking about it's part first person  shooter part visual novel part card game  and part  speed running tutorial picking up soul  cards gives you access to weapons to  take out demons that have infested  heaven but by burning the cards you get  access to abilities like bombs or a  double jump which will help you complete  the levels even faster the entire game  is built to teach you how to complete  its levels as quickly as you can and  it's incredibly satisfying to unlock ace  medals find each secret and crucially  climb those leaderboards  if you like a schlocky horror game that  wears its references proudly on its  sleeve then the quarry is one for you  made by supermassive games the team  behind until dawn it throws another  group of teens into a scary situation  that not all of them will escape whether  you play alone with others or just set  up some settings so the game makes the  decisions for you and plays out like a  movie the quarry is full of scares and  gruesome moments that will keep you  entertained throughout its run time  regarded as the best kirby game yet  kirby and the forgotten land burst onto  the switch in early 2022. it revitalized  the usual kirby formula with mouthful  mode where he inhales big items like  cars and his body stretches to  accommodate not only is it very funny to  see kirby waddle around as a big cone  but it freshens gameplay by offering new  mechanics throw in delightful puzzles  and platforming and kirby and the  forgotten land is a game for fans young  and old alike  ghost ride tokyo comes from the  development studio behind the evil  within and while it may not be jump out  of your seat scary it's a slow burn of  supernatural spooks mixed with a unique  combat system that packs a punch as  akito you're brought back from the dead  by a mischievous spirit called kk who  grants you access to his powers while  the two of you team up to find out just  what's up with a mysterious fog that's  covered tokyo  horizon forbidden west is the sequel to  2017's zero dawn and once again follows  eloy as she and her companions attempt  to fix a world that was broken by greedy  corporations and a misfiring ai in  forbidden west she travels well  west to find the ancient tech that will  fix earth's biosphere and stop a blight  that threatens to destroy all life if  you enjoyed zero dawn then forbidden  west is more of the same but with more  to do and more characters to get to know  and love  while tunic might remind you of older  legend of zelda titles from its  isometric perspective plus its green  garbed protagonist that has a sword and  shield it actually has more in common  with souls games with tough stamina  based combat and rest points that  respawn enemies tunic requires a lot of  your attention it also has beautiful  level design and also similarly to souls  games doesn't really tell you where to  go or what you should be doing while you  can tune its difficulty in menus you  need to invest time in the game and  collect lost pages from an instruction  manual to piece it all together  speaking of souls like games what is  there to say about elden ring that  hasn't been said already i'm not going  to belabor the point but if souls games  haven't been your thing before i implore  you to give this one a try if its  difficulty is off-putting try an  astrologer build or make great use of  its summoning pools hell even cheese  those bad boys it's a tough game but  it's so rewarding and features some of  the best open world design ever there is  a reason  actually many reasons that it's so  lorded  this one is a real trust me don't look  up anything about this game  recommendation not only would it spoil  the experience it's also just quite  difficult to explain the concept the  stanley parable launched in 2013 but was  updated this year with the ultra deluxe  edition which basically acts as a sequel  to the original a wonderful mix of humor  and commentary on how we play and enjoy  games the stanley parable ultra deluxe  edition is a real must play  okay switch sports may not have all of  the sports of wii sports and wii sports  resort but there's still something  wonderfully nostalgic about seeing me's  bowling together the game features  football tennis bowling badminton  chambara and volleyball with golf due to  be added as a free update later this  year if you want to climb the ranks and  best your buds on the court then this is  the one for you  since its launch in 2017 destiny 2 has  received frequent massive updates and  2022's the witch queen was just that  featuring a ton of new content from  missions and gear to a whole new raid  while the story might go over the heads  of new players who maybe haven't watched  a recap first returning players will be  rewarded with some of the game's best  story moments yet  nobody saves the world is a dungeon  crawler with one of the most satisfying  gameplay loops i've experienced starting  the game as the eponymous nobody quickly  you gain a magic wand and the ability to  shapeshift into different creatures and  characters you can be a rat or a massive  dragon but each form has useful and  unique abilities and you can mix and  match them to create customized builds  you can either play alone or with a  friend but regardless it's a wild  adventure  if you want to shoot nazis in the dick  then boy do i have the game for you  sniper elite 5 is the latest in  rebellion's long running series and  while it'll be familiar fair if you've  played one before there are plenty of  new additions like more in-depth weapon  customization and multiplayer invasions  to keep it feeling fresh and interesting  teenage mutant ninja turtles shredders  revenge walks a tight line of retaining  the feel of the classic beat-em-up games  that the turtles appeared in while also  freshening up the formula for a 2022  audience the result is a game that's a  love letter to all things tmnt but also  feels fantastic to play it's packed full  of easter eggs for turtles fans to  uncover and it's an absolute blast to  play in co-op with friends just be  warned you'll be hearing that theme song  in your head for days afterwards  norco is very different to most other  games on this list both in terms of  gameplay and aesthetic but it's one that  certainly shouldn't be missed a  point-and-click adventure game set in  south louisiana norco's story is set  around k who returns to the town to sort  through the affairs of her recently  deceased mother and to track down her  missing brother the story starts simply  but quickly a huge mystery begins to  unravel around kaye and her family  dystopian whimsical and dark this  adventure game will stick with you long  after the credits have rolled don't miss  it  okay this one is technically cheating  because monster hunter rise came out  last year on the nintendo switch however  2022 saw its pc release which our  reviewer richard wakeling calls the  definitive version monster hunter as a  franchise is absolutely massive just  look at its sales figures and steam  concurrents but it has been accused of  being unwelcoming to new players  something that has been somewhat  remedied by ryze's more approachable  nature you still kill giant monsters but  now it's easier and quicker to get into  the action the pc port delivers high  quality textures and it runs much more  smoothly than its nintendo switch  counterpart it's on this list not only  because it's a fantastic port but  because of the huge new sunbreak  expansion which adds new quests areas  monsters and a new big monster to hunt  the elder dragon malzino if you've been  wary of playing monster hunter before  now this is the time to jump in  there you have it 15 of the best games  released this year so far there are  plenty of huge exciting releases set to  come including call of duty modern  warfare gotham knights and the callisto  protocol we'll always have the latest  sofa more on these games and even more  drop us a like and subscribe to gamespot  on youtube i'm on twitter at lucy james  games and i'll catch you next time
 

